# Beats script: what's left before launch (DLG-1, docs/plans/dialogue-stage.md section 3). Seconds: launch.json.
# Read it top to bottom as the conversation. "# you" lines are the person; every other line is what the agent sends.
# A reply is one flow (meta.flow, one row per beat). A beat opens with its spoken line (say) and holds what that line
# changes on screen. The timeline is sent whole in beat 1; each later beat moves the row it names.

# you: What's left before launch?

# reply 1, flow l1
# beat 1
say "Three cards are left before launch."
anchor "3 cards left"
timeline@launch "Before launch"
next@memory "Memory check"
next@barge "Barge-in"
next@guide "Guide rewrite"
# beat 2
say "The memory check is green, no leaks across five agents."
anchor "Memory check: green"
~memory kind=done sub="no leaks"
# beat 3
say "Barge-in is in test, but only on the simulator so far."
anchor "Barge-in: in test"
~barge kind=now sub="in test, sim only"
# you cut in during beat 3: is that the echo problem?

# reply 2, flow l2
# beat 4
say "Yes. The phone can hear its own voice, so it needs a test at full volume."
~barge sub="echo test at full volume next"
# beat 5
say "The guide rewrite has not started yet."
anchor "Guide rewrite: not started"
~guide sub="not started"
# beat 6
say "Which one should go first?"
wait@first "Which one first?" "Barge-in"|"Guide rewrite" +in
# you, touching the Guide rewrite row: the guide

# reply 3, flow l3
# beat 7
say "Guide rewrite goes first. It moves to now, and I start it today."
anchor "Now: guide rewrite"
~guide kind=now sub="starts today"
